# FIRST Display Review: N15 Choices, Batch 1

Status: PASS for the explicitly observed rendered regions only.

Fresh review of the eight assigned existing desktop 1440 x 960 PNGs. Each was opened exactly once with native `view_image`, after all eight SHA-256 values matched the assignment. No previous observations were read or inherited.

## Observations

| PNG | Observed regions | Rendered evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1440-choices-0001.png | Q1-Q2 stems and A-D; Q3 stem and A-B | Legible inequalities, letter lists, braces and arrows. Q3 prose wraps to visible final sentences. Q1 final option letters are e/d/a/d; Q2 final comparisons are q > m, q < m, q > m, q < m. |
| 1440-choices-0002.png | Q3 B-D; Q4 stem and A-E; Q5 stem and A-D | Ordered labels and complete sentence tails. Q4 final formula terms include b + 1, b, b + 8 and b − 2; D's determination sentence is complete. Q5 A wraps to a visible final line. |
| 1440-choices-0003.png | Q6-Q8 stems and A-D | All Q6 station sequences end visibly at Riverton. Q7 stacked fraction endpoints are 1, 1/10, 1/2, 1. Q8 final values are −10, 0, −1, −1; D is readable close to the bottom. |
| 1440-choices-0004.png | Q8 D; Q9-Q11 stems and A-D | Readable fractions, decimals, inequality signs and superscripts. Q9 tails are −5/6, −5/6, −0.83, −5/6; Q10 tails are 2¹⁰, 33², 6⁴, 6⁴. Q11 final maximum-value statements are visible. |
| 1440-choices-0005.png | Q11 D; Q12 stem, figure and A-F | Complete f/g/h figure with readable a/b/c labels, visible nodes, paths, loops and arrowheads. The rightmost h region, including b and c, is inside the image. Six ordered option sentences are complete. |
| 1440-choices-0006.png | Q13 stem, figure and A-C; Q14 stem and A-C | Complete f/g/h figure and f/g/h option rows. Q14's stem wraps visibly rather than losing a horizontal tail. A-C have complete fractions and final ≥ 0, ≥ 0, ≤ 0 tails. |
| 1440-choices-0007.png | Q14 D; Q15-Q16 stems and A-D; Q17 stem and A-C | Q14 D is complete here. Q15/Q16 denominators and sign/zero tails are readable. Q17's product has visible closing parentheses and its final prose line is complete; A-C show (a − b)/(a + b), 1, −1. |
| 1440-choices-0008.png | Q17 A-D; Q18-Q19 stems and A-D | Q17 D visibly shows (a − 3b)/(a + b). Q18/Q19 parenthesized fractions, inner/outer exponents, right formula boundaries and final prose are readable. All option denominators and superscripts are visible. |

No horizontal missing-tail finding was observed in these complete regions. No endpoints were reconstructed from mathematics. `result.json` binds each PASS terminal fact to its image hash and question, option or figure region. Slash notation transcribes stacked fractions; superscript characters transcribe rendered powers.

## Coverage Exclusions

- 0001: Q3 C-D are below the viewport.
- 0002: Q3 stem/A are above the viewport; Q6 is only a bottom vertical fragment.
- 0004: Q8 C intersects the top edge; its stem/A-B are above the viewport.
- 0005: The preceding Q11 C formula fragment intersects the top edge; its stem/A-B are absent. Q13 begins at the bottom boundary, with its figure/options outside this viewport.
- 0006: Q14 D intersects the bottom edge; no complete fraction or terminal fact is claimed for that row here.
- 0007: Q14 C intersects the top edge and its stem/A-B are absent; Q17 D is below the viewport.
- 0008: Q17's stem formula intersects the top edge and its heading is absent.

These are vertical coverage exclusions, not horizontal-tail defects. They do not approve absent or clipped content. Complete regions observed in another assigned PNG have their own fresh, hash-bound observations.

## Controls and Limits

Visible single/multiple-choice mode text and ordered option labels were inspected. No separate radio, checkbox or action-button controls are visible in these PNGs; interactive-control rendering and behavior are not approved.

This review does not judge mathematics, source fidelity, solutions, answers, or full-lesson readiness. It used no other images, sources, keys, browser, capture, render, crop, resize, reopen, network, database, paid service or installation. Only this batch's three owned reports were written. Token and cost usage are UNKNOWN.
